---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About The Japan Filter -- who publishes it, how it works, and how guides are researched.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 py-14">

    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl text-indigo mb-10">About The Japan Filter</h1>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-indigo mt-10 mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-line">What this site is</h2>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 mb-4">
      The Japan Filter looks at products that are well regarded in Japan's
      domestic market and re-checks them for buyers outside the country.
    </p>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
      Being popular in Japan does not automatically make something a good buy
      abroad. The model sold overseas is often a different unit, the warranty
      may not apply, and the price gap can be substantial. This site exists to
      find those gaps before you spend money.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-indigo mt-10 mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-line">Who publishes it</h2>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 mb-4">
      The Japan Filter is written and published by a sole proprietor operating
      under the trade name 408Consulting, based in Miyagi Prefecture, Japan.
    </p>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
      Reading Japanese retail listings, manufacturer specification sheets, and
      domestic review data is ordinary daily activity here, not a research trip.
      That is the reason this site can exist: most of the source material is in
      Japanese and never gets translated.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-indigo mt-10 mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-line">What we do</h2>
    <ul class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 space-y-2 pl-0 list-none">
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="shrink-0 font-data text-[11px] font-medium text-seal mt-0.5">--</span>
        <span>Compare the Japanese-market model against the version sold on Amazon.com, specification by specification</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="shrink-0 font-data text-[11px] font-medium text-seal mt-0.5">--</span>
        <span>Read manufacturer documentation in Japanese for warranty terms, country of manufacture, and model differences</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="shrink-0 font-data text-[11px] font-medium text-seal mt-0.5">--</span>
        <span>Use Japanese domestic retail and review data for context that US listings leave out</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="shrink-0 font-data text-[11px] font-medium text-seal mt-0.5">--</span>
        <span>Confirm a product is genuinely available through official US channels before recommending it</span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-indigo mt-10 mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-line">What we do not do</h2>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 mb-4">
      We are not a testing lab. We do not buy, use, or physically test the
      products covered here, and no guide on this site will claim that we did.
    </p>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 mb-4">
      Every guide includes a section called "How We Researched This Guide"
      stating exactly what its conclusions rest on. Where a claim comes from a
      manufacturer's own documentation rather than independent evidence, we
      say so in the guide.
    </p>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
      We would rather tell you what we actually know than imply more.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-indigo mt-10 mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-line">Not every verdict is a recommendation</h2>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
      Some guides conclude that a product is not worth buying, or not worth
      buying from outside Japan. When that happens we say so directly and point
      to an alternative. A site that recommends everything is not filtering
      anything.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-indigo mt-10 mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-line">How this site makes money</h2>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 mb-4">
      The Japan Filter participates in the Amazon Associates Program and earns
      commission on qualifying purchases made through links on this site. This
      costs you nothing extra.
    </p>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
      It does not affect our conclusions. We have no relationship with any brand
      covered here, receive no products from them, and are not paid by them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-indigo mt-10 mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-line">Corrections</h2>
    <p class="font-body text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
      Specifications change, models get discontinued, and we make mistakes.
      If you find something wrong, write to
      <a href="mailto:hello@thejapanfilter.com" class="text-indigo underline hover:text-indigo/70">hello@thejapanfilter.com</a>
      and we will correct it.
    </p>

  </article>
</BaseLayout>
